# Oblivious Bookworm: "you turned a permanent face up this turn" (CR 701.40b, 708.8), read as the ability resolves - so a
# permanent turned face up with the trigger on the stack counts (the ruling: only once it begins to resolve is it too
# late). The face-down permanent entered on turn 1, not this turn: only the turning up can make the "unless" hold.
#
# Turn 1: Black Lotus for {R}{R}{R}, Mox Emerald for Llanowar Elves, Turn Inside Out on them and Lightning Bolt: they die
# and manifest dread puts a second Llanowar Elves onto the battlefield face down. Turn 3 Bot1 draws the Forest, plays it
# and casts the Bookworm with Mox Sapphire. At the end step, with the Bookworm's trigger on the stack, Bot1 turns the
# manifested Elves face up for {G} from Mox Emerald (a special action, no stack). Then it draws Counterspell and keeps it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Llanowar Elves
Turn Inside Out
Lightning Bolt
Oblivious Bookworm
Llanowar Elves
Island
Forest
Counterspell
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Turn Inside Out.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Llanowar Elves | Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivious Bookworm.Cast
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
Bot1.Battlefield.#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.FaceDown = (absent)
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Hand = Counterspell
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
